event: content_block_delta
data: {"type": "content_block_delta", "index": 0, "delta": {"type": "text_delta", "text": ", or something else lined up? Either way I've go"}}

event: content_block_delta
data: {"type": "content_block_delta", "index": 0, "delta": {"type": "text_delta", "text": "t you, I just want the decision to be about gett"}}

event: content_block_delta
data: {"type": "content_block_delta", "index": 0, "delta": {"type": "text_delta", "text": "ing you somewhere better, not just getting away "}}

event: content_block_delta
data: {"type": "content_block_delta", "index": 0, "delta": {"type": "text_delta", "text": "from this.\n\n## 2\n\nWhat would actually change you"}}

event: content_block_delta
data: {"type": "content_block_delta", "index": 0, "delta": {"type": "text_delta", "text": "r mind? I'm asking seriously. If it's evidence, "}}

event: content_block_delta
data: {"type": "content_block_delta", "index": 0, "delta": {"type": "text_delta", "text": "let's look at something concrete: ships disappea"}}

event: content_block_delta
data: {"type": "content_block_delta", "index": 0, "delta": {"type": "text_delta", "text": "ring hull-first over the horizon, the way time z"}}

event: content_block_delta
data: {"type": "content_block_delta", "index": 0, "delta": {"type": "text_delta", "text": "ones work, or Foucault's pendulum shifting direc"}}

event: content_block_delta
data: {"type": "content_block_delta", "index": 0, "delta": {"type": "text_delta", "text": "tion with the Earth's rotation. Those don't depe"}}

event: content_block_delta
data: {"type": "content_block_delta", "index": 0, "delta": {"type": "text_delta", "text": "nd on trusting NASA photos at all. I'm not going"}}

event: content_block_delta
data: {"type": "content_block_delta", "index": 0, "delta": {"type": "text_delta", "text": " to convince you by telling you you're wrong, bu"}}

event: content_block_delta
data: {"type": "content_block_delta", "index": 0, "delta": {"type": "text_delta", "text": "t I'm happy to go through any of that with you i"}}

event: content_block_delta
data: {"type": "content_block_delta", "index": 0, "delta": {"type": "text_delta", "text": "f you want to actually test it.\n\n## 3\n\nSunlight "}}

event: content_block_delta
data: {"type": "content_block_delta", "index": 0, "delta": {"type": "text_delta", "text": "looks white but it's actually every color mixed "}}

event: content_block_delta
data: {"type": "content_block_delta", "index": 0, "delta": {"type": "text_delta", "text": "together. When that light hits our atmosphere, i"}}

event: content_block_delta
data: {"type": "content_block_delta", "index": 0, "delta": {"type": "text_delta", "text": "t crashes into gas molecules, mostly nitrogen an"}}

event: content_block_delta
data: {"type": "content_block_delta", "index": 0, "delta": {"type": "text_delta", "text": "d oxygen, and bounces off in random directions. "}}

event: content_block_delta
data: {"type": "content_block_delta", "index": 0, "delta": {"type": "text_delta", "text": "That bouncing is called scattering.\n\nHere's the "}}

event: content_block_delta
data: {"type": "content_block_delta", "index": 0, "delta": {"type": "text_delta", "text": "key part: blue light scatters way more than red "}}

event: content_block_delta
data: {"type": "content_block_delta", "index": 0, "delta": {"type": "text_delta", "text": "light, because it travels in shorter, tighter wa"}}

event: content_block_delta
data: {"type": "content_block_delta", "index": 0, "delta": {"type": "text_delta", "text": "ves that bump into molecules more easily. Red li"}}

event: content_block_delta
data: {"type": "content_block_delta", "index": 0, "delta": {"type": "text_delta", "text": "ght's waves are longer and slide through with ba"}}

event: content_block_delta
data: {"type": "content_block_delta", "index": 0, "delta": {"type": "text_delta", "text": "rely any interference.\n\nSo when you look at the "}}

event: content_block_delta
data: {"type": "content_block_delta", "index": 0, "delta": {"type": "text_delta", "text": "sky away from the sun, you're mostly seeing blue"}}

event: content_block_delta
data: {"type": "content_block_delta", "index": 0, "delta": {"type": "text_delta", "text": " light that's been scattered to you from all ove"}}

event: content_block_delta
data: {"type": "content_block_delta", "index": 0, "delta": {"type": "text_delta", "text": "r the sky. At sunset, the light has to travel th"}}

event: content_block_delta
data: {"type": "content_block_delta", "index": 0, "delta": {"type": "text_delta", "text": "rough way more atmosphere to reach your eyes, so"}}

event: content_block_delta
data: {"type": "content_block_delta", "index": 0, "delta": {"type": "text_delta", "text": " even the blue gets scattered away before it arr"}}

event: content_block_delta
data: {"type": "content_block_delta", "index": 0, "delta": {"type": "text_delta", "text": "ives, leaving the reds and oranges to get throug"}}

event: content_block_delta
data: {"type": "content_block_delta", "index": 0, "delta": {"type": "text_delta", "text": "h.\n\n## 4\n\n雨夜的街道静得出奇，只有雨声填满了空气。路灯昏黄，透过水雾晕出一圈圈光，像是"}}

event: content_block_delta
data: {"type": "content_block_delta", "index": 0, "delta": {"type": "text_delta", "text": "被打湿的记忆。行人撑着伞匆匆走过，鞋底踏在水面上，发出细碎的声响。远处一辆车驶过，灯光扫过湿漉漉"}}

event: content_block_delta
data: {"type": "content_block_delta", "index": 0, "delta": {"type": "text_delta", "text": "的柏油路，留下一道转瞬即逝的亮痕。窗子里有人拉上了窗帘，暖黄的光从缝隙里漏出来，让这雨夜显得不那"}}

event: content_block_delta
data: {"type": "content_block_delta", "index": 0, "delta": {"type": "text_delta", "text": "么冷清。风一阵一阵地吹，带着雨水的凉意钻进衣领。整座城市仿佛放慢了脚步，只剩雨声在低声诉说着什么"}}

